# Line-ending policy for NemesisBot Rust sources.
#
# Force LF for *.rs regardless of core.autocrlf. The repo already stores *.rs
# blobs as LF (core.autocrlf=true strips CRLF on commit); this attribute makes
# checkouts produce LF working trees too, so rustfmt output (LF) and git agree
# and the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" churn for Rust files disappears.
#
# *.rs first, then *.sh (2026-10-20): shell scripts only ever execute under
# bash (git-bash / Linux / WSL), where CRLF breaks parsing — the B7 WSL image
# build route hit exactly this (autocrlf checkout turned build-vm-image.sh
# CRLF; WSL bash read `set -euo pipefail\r` and rejected `pipefail` as an
# invalid option name). Pinning *.sh to LF keeps every checkout runnable.
# .bat/.ps1 stay CRLF (Windows-native interpreters).
*.rs text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
